{
  "l1pq": "Read the following passage, which paraphrases a description of the Thesmophoria festival:\n\n'For five days each autumn, the women of Athens left their homes and set up camps near a sanctuary. No man was permitted to enter. The women who could afford it paid for the animals to be sacrificed; others carried out the sacred rites connected with the earth and with the story of Persephone. The festival had to be organised and funded by the women themselves.'\n\nWhat does this passage reveal about the religious roles available to Athenian women? Use details from the passage in your answer.",
